.TH MIGRATOR 8 "2026-11-21" "migrator 1.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
migrator \- move a Linux server onto this machine over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B migrator
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-y ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR keyfile ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR disk [ ,disk2 ]]
.RB [ \-s
.IR step ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR key = value ]...
.RI [ donor ]
.RI [ arg ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B migrator
copies a complete Linux installation from a donor machine onto the machine it
runs on, then makes the copy bootable.
It reads the state of both machines, writes a migration plan that can be
inspected and edited before anything is written, recreates the donor's disk
layout on the target, streams every file system over the network, repairs the
copy inside a chroot (fstab, initramfs drivers, boot loader, network settings)
and verifies the result before the switch-over.
The donor's disks are only ever read.
.PP
Both modes assume the two machines are connected over the network.
In the off-line mode both are booted into the migration Live, a self-contained
environment that carries this tool and the utilities it needs.
In the on-line mode the donor keeps serving:
.B migrator-agent
is copied to the donor, the volumes are copied in passes while the file
systems stay in use, and only the remaining differences are frozen for the
final copy.
.PP
Root is required: the tool partitions disks and mounts file systems.
Run it with no arguments to perform the whole migration, or with
.B \-s
to run a single step.
Steps are idempotent, so a failed step can be repeated without starting over.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Print every command that would be run and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-y
Answer yes to every confirmation.
.TP
.BI \-i " keyfile"
Use this SSH key for the donor instead of the session key migrator generates.
.TP
.BI \-d " disk"
Target disk on this machine, for example
.IR /dev/sda ,
.I /dev/nvme0n1
or a
.I /dev/disk/by-id/...
path.
Defaults to the only eligible disk; if several qualify, migrator refuses and
lists them.
With
.B \-o raid=1
two disks are named as
.IR disk , disk2 .
.TP
.BI \-s " step"
Run one step only.
The accepted values are listed under STEPS.
.TP
.BI \-o " key=value"
Set one option.
Repeat the flag for every key; a comma belongs to the value
.RB ( driver=mod1,mod2 ),
so keys are never joined by one.
An unknown key is refused rather than ignored.
The keys are listed under OPTION KEYS.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Print the built-in help and exit.
.SH STEPS
.TP
.B plan " donor"
Read both machines without writing anything and write the plan.
.TP
.B check " [plan]"
Re-validate a plan, including one that was edited by hand.
.TP
.B apply
Partition and format the target disks and start the initial synchronisation.
.TP
.B transfer
Copy the file systems.
.TP
.B postfix " [root]"
Repair the copy in a chroot: fstab, mdadm, initramfs, boot loader, network.
.TP
.B verify " [root]"
Run the verification items and, with
.BR boottest=1 ,
boot the copy in qemu.
.TP
.B cutover
Stop the donor and switch the network identity over to this machine.
.TP
.B inventory " [donor]"
Print the raw records of this machine, or of the donor.
.TP
.B attach
Reattach to the running tmux session, or follow its log.
.TP
.B cleanup
Undo the mounts, activations and read-only marks left behind by a run.
.SH OPTION KEYS
Keys accepted in both modes:
.TP
.BR root=auto|block|files
How the root file system is identified in the copy.
.TP
.BR label=auto|gpt|dos
Partition table type on the target.
.TP
.BR nic=IFACE
Network interface name in the copy.
.TP
.BR donor-nic=IFACE " and " nic-pin=1|0
Interface to expect on the donor, and whether the name is pinned.
.TP
.BR driver=MOD , console=... , bootorder=pxe|local
Kernel driver, console and boot order of the copy.
.TP
.BR boottest=1|0
Boot the copy in qemu and wait for multi-user on a serial console.
Needs
.BR qemu-system-x86 ,
which is installed on demand; the target disk is never written.
.TP
.BR fsck=quick|full , boot-part=SIZE
File system check depth and size of the boot partition.
.TP
.BR cutover=netdown|poweroff|kexec|none
How the donor is stopped at the end.
.TP
.BR force=1
Continue where a mismatch would otherwise stop the run.
.TP
.BR raw=DIR , cipher=..., expect=SERIAL|MAC
Raw mode, SSH cipher and the identity to expect.
.TP
.BR relay=USER@HOST[:PORT]
Route the copy through a relay host.
.TP
.BR raid=1
Mirror two identical disks with md RAID1; the boot loader and ESP are written
to both.
On-line mode only:
.TP
.BR chunk=SIZE , passes=N , converge=N , max-est=N
Copy granularity and the bounds on the convergence loop.
.TP
.BR tracker=auto|bpf|ftrace
How block writes on the donor are tracked.
.TP
.BR stall=SECONDS , settle=MILLISECONDS
Silence that counts as a wedged connection, and the delay before a pass starts.
.TP
.BR precheck=1|0 , precheck-dir=DIR , precheck-cow=SIZE
Run postfix and verify on a snapshot of the copy while the donor keeps running.
.TP
.BR patience=SECONDS
Extra copying time to trade for a shorter freeze.
.TP
.BR verify-hash=1 , cutover-port=PORT , dpkg-wait=SECONDS
Hash every frozen volume, the port used for the switch-over, and how long to
let an interrupted package operation on the donor finish before the freeze.
.TP
.BR compress=auto|zstd[:LEVEL]|lz4|none
Compression of the stream; off-line mode uses lz4 by default.
Off-line mode only:
.TP
.BR data=ssh|raw , sshd-port=PORT , watchdog=SECONDS
Transport of the copy, the port the donor listens on, and the watchdog timeout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, environment or identity problem; nothing was written.
.TP
.B 3
Verification failed.
The target disk has been written: do not boot it.
.TP
.B 4
The plan is infeasible, or a hand-edited plan was rejected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUN
Session directory, default
.IR /run/migrator .
It holds the plan, the state of the run and the log.
.TP
.B MIGRATOR_LIB
Directory holding the shell libraries.
Set automatically from the location of the program; override it only when the
libraries live elsewhere.
.TP
.B MIGRATOR_AGENT
Path to
.BR migrator-agent ,
used instead of the search beside the libraries and on
.SM PATH .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/migrator/plan
The migration plan, written by the
.B plan
step and editable before
.BR apply .
.TP
.I /run/migrator/state
What the run has completed so far; this is what makes the steps idempotent.
.TP
.I /run/migrator/log
Transcript of the run.
.PP
The session directory is on a tmpfs, so it does not survive a reboot.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the whole migration, taking the donor address from the command line:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
migrator root@10.0.0.12
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read both machines and inspect the plan first:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
migrator \-s plan root@10.0.0.12
$EDITOR /run/migrator/plan
migrator \-s check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Turn compression off and allow five convergence passes:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
migrator \-o compress=none \-o converge=5 root@10.0.0.12
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR partclone (8),
.BR mdadm (8),
.BR lvm (8)
.PP
The full documentation, including the option reference and the acceptance
checks, is in the project wiki at
.IR https://github.com/tktogether/migrator/wiki .
